  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Migration is a moral issue for Burnham – but he also wants to tell a positive story",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/02/migration-andy-burnham-shabana-mahmood-labour-immigration",
      "description": "<p>While PM is keen to support those making a contribution his backing of Shabana Mahmood’s hard line is no surprise</p><p>While out on the campaign trail in Makerfield, Andy Burnham <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/jun/04/i-wouldnt-flinch-burnham-on-social-care-markets-brexit-and-the-prospect-of-a-general-election\">gave a glimpse</a> into where he might land on Labour’s plans for immigration reform, which had already been decried by the left of the party as unfair and the right as electorally necessary.</p><p>Asked by the Guardian what he thought of Reform’s attack on “open borders Andy” – Nigel Farage’s early attempt to define him as soft on migration – the then Manchester mayor dismissed the charge as “ridiculous” and went on the defensive.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/02/migration-andy-burnham-shabana-mahmood-labour-immigration\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-02T20:39:52"
    },
    {
      "title": "Shabana Mahmood softens immigration plans in face of cabinet backlash",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/02/shabana-mahmood-softens-immigration-plans-cabinet-backlash-leave-to-remain",
      "description": "<p>Exception for care workers will allow an estimated 280,000 people and their dependants to apply for indefinite leave to remain after five years</p><p>Shabana Mahmood rowed back on her most hardline plans to make care workers wait 15 years for settlement in the UK, but told MPs on Monday that many migrants would still face retrospective rule changes to make them wait a decade.</p><p>Under pressure from a cabinet backlash and health unions, the home secretary has offered a carve-out for care workers to allow them to apply for indefinite leave to remain after five years.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/nov/02/shabana-mahmood-softens-immigration-plans-cabinet-backlash-leave-to-remain\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-02T19:06:40"
    },
    {
      "title": "Charities condemn proposal to make some refugees wait up to 30 years for settlement – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/nov/02/andy-burnham-shabana-mahmood-migration-indefinite-leave-to-remain-care-workers-uk-politics-latest-news",
      "description": "<p>Executive director of external affairs at the<strong> </strong>Refugee Council called the proposals ‘unfair and unworkable’ </p><p>Downing Street has declined to say how much it cost for the plane carrying Andy Burnham and UK delegates to a Commonwealth leaders’ summit to stop in Manchester to pick him up (see <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/nov/02/andy-burnham-shabana-mahmood-migration-indefinite-leave-to-remain-care-workers-uk-politics-latest-news?page=with%3Ablock-6ae865238f08964d851be7a5#block-6ae865238f08964d851be7a5\">10.28am</a>), the Press Association reports.</p><p>At the morning lobby briefing, asked if this was an appropriate use of public money, the <strong>PM’s spokesperson</strong> said:</p><p>The prime minister’s travel arrangements are made on the basis of security, operational requirements, and value for money for the taxpayer.</p><p>The prime minister’s travel arrangements reflect where he was carrying out official government business at the end of last week.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/nov/02/andy-burnham-shabana-mahmood-migration-indefinite-leave-to-remain-care-workers-uk-politics-latest-news\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-02T18:38:22"
    },
    {
      "title": "UK government waters down proposals for legal migration",
